  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "近代建築史",
    "sub_ename": "HISTORY OF MODERN ARCHITECTURE",
    "describe_ch": "本課程主要在討論從啟蒙運動到第一次世界大戰後在西方建築史上的發展歷程。在本課程中，我們所關切的是近代建築思潮的發展脈絡以及其相關文化和社會上的議題。尤其是如何看待建築學與藝術、科學和哲學等不同學門之間的發展與影響。本課程要求學生熟悉該時期建築風格主義、建築大師與代表作品，並且能夠查詢與閱讀相關建築作品與論述。",
    "describe_eh": "This course discusses the developments and trends of Western architecture from the Enlightenment to World War I. We concern the issues on early modern architecture in related to the cultural and social background.  In particular, we observe the developments and changes in the field of architecture from the influences of art, science and philosophy. Students are required to be familiar with architectural style, isms, masters and representative works and read related architectural literature.",
    "pre_subname": "ARCH2303西洋建築史",
    "pre_sub_id3": "ARCH2303",
    "pre_sub_ename": "ARCH2303 A HISTORY OF WESTERN  ARCHITECTURE",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "對於近代建築史的思潮發展、建築大師及其作品能夠有系統性的認識。能夠區分近代建築史中如：新藝術、風格派、包浩斯、國際式樣等在思潮與作品上的特色，增進對於近代建築發展之國際觀。",
      "describe_en": "Students are able to acknowledge the trends, masters and masterpieces of the history of early modern architecture systematically and to distinguish the characteristics of various styles, e.g. Art Nouveau, De Stijl, Bauhaus and International Style. They al"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "思考建築史在建築設計過程中的重要性，同時透過課程的訓練，能將所學應用在建築設計上。",
      "describe_en": "Students can understand the importance of architectural history on the process of design, and apply it into architectural design."
    }
  ],
